<title>USA: SanDisk wins HP supplier deal.</title>
<headline>SanDisk wins HP supplier deal.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>SanDisk Corp on Monday said it has been chosen to supply CompactFlash memory storage cards to Hewlett-Packard Co for use in HP's new palmtop computer, the the HP 320LX.</p>
<p>CompactFlash is a miniature storage card developed by SanDisk that is widely used for small, removable storage.</p>
<p>Financial terms of the supply deal were undisclosed.</p>
